Consequently:

1. every old vertex outside \(M_e\) has \(\lambda_e(p)=1\);
2. every beta parent \(p\in M_e\) must satisfy

   $$
   m_{pL}+m_{pR}<m_e(p),
   \qquad
   \lambda_e(p)
   =
   \frac{m_e(p)}
        {m_e(p)-m_{pL}-m_{pR}},
   \tag{118.3}
   $$

   where \(m_e(p)=\mathsf G_e(p,p)\) and
   \(m_{p\sigma}=\mathsf G_c(p\sigma,p\sigma)\).

